From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: align SM8150 encoder controls

Port the remaining standard encoder-control policy required by the
downstream SM8150 Venus 4xx firmware contract.

Wire rotation and flipping, H.264 sample aspect ratio, HEVC tier, packed
per-frame QP ranges, base-layer priority, VBV/low-latency policy and
multi-slice configuration.  Preserve the downstream property ordering and
correct the HFI4 QP-range and vertical-flip payload encodings.  Keep work
mode separate from low-latency configuration, as required by the vendor
startup sequence.

Do not expose H264_I_PERIOD on IRIS1: the firmware interface provides IDR
period and P-frame count but no exact equivalent for the V4L2 open-GOP
I-period control, so accepting it would be a silent no-op.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
